//! Golden test for `pr_core::file_actions::service`: every case of `tests/golden/file-action-scenarios.json` (111 cases:
//! 56 single, 55 group), generated by the C# oracle `W304Disk` / `W304Bin` at baseline d92d6aae (contract W3-04,
//! "Golden package"). Red until the W3-04 bodies land.
//!
//! The harness reproduces the oracle's fake disk ([`ScenarioFs`], over `pr_test_support::FakeFileSystem`) and bin
//! ([`GoldenBin`], over the shared [`ScenarioBin`]) and compares, per case: the result fields, the journal lines after
//! GUID normalization (`<id1>`, `<id2>`, ... in order of first appearance over the journal lines, then `group_id`, then
//! `entry.id` / `entry.group_id`), `journal_ends_with_crlf`, `files_after`, `dirs_after`, `recycled`,
//! `permanently_deleted_paths`, `fits_calls`, the hook `trace`, `busy_after` and `token_cancelled`.
//!
//! Semantics of the fault keys (`faults`), as the names and the golden expectations pin them:
//! * `move_fail` / `copy_fail` / `delete_fail` / `recycle_fail` / `permanent_fail`: `{path: message}`, the call fails
//!   before anything changes (the message is the error text);
//! * `move_leaves_source`: the move copies, the source stays; `move_truncate`: the move, then the destination is cut to N
//!   bytes; `move_round_2s`: the moved destination's stamp is floored to an even second (FAT);
//! * `copy_partial`: `{path: {bytes, message}}`, N bytes are written, then the call fails; `copy_size`: a complete copy
//!   of N bytes succeeds (a short copy); `foreign_on_copy`: `{path: N}`, a foreign N-byte file appears at the destination
//!   and the copy fails with "already exists"; `copy_then_cancel`: the copy completes, then the token is cancelled;
//! * `recycle_leaves` / `permanent_leaves`: the call succeeds, the file stays;
//! * `append_fail`: 1-based indices of journal appends that fail with "journal unavailable";
//! * `cancel_on`: `{op, path}`: the token is cancelled when that traced call starts, then the call is performed;
//! * `pre_cancelled`: the token is cancelled before the action; `move_override`: `move-then-fail` / `move-then-cancel`.
//!
//! TODO(W3-04, lead): `tools/oracle-cs/Commands/W3-04.cs` is not in the tree yet (the contract says it is copied from the
//! package), so these semantics are read from the golden names and expectations, not from `W304Disk`. Check them against
//! the oracle when that file lands; a mismatch is a harness bug, not a service bug.

mod common_file_actions;

